What is Collection Interface?
The Collection is an interface in the Java Collection Framework.

It is the parent interface for List, Set, and Queue.

It provides common methods to store and manage groups of objects.

Why Collection Interface?

Imagine Java has three different data structures:
List
Set
Queue
All of them need common operations like:

Add data
Remove data
Check data
Find size

Instead of writing the same methods in every interface, Java created one common interface called
